      'pr.about.h': 'About Sassembly',
      'pr.about.b': 'Sassembly is a royalty-free instruction set architecture and systems language whose keywords are Sanskrit words and whose operand roles are marked by kāraka sigils rather than by position or punctuation. Its compiler is written in Sassembly.',
      'pr.verify.h': 'Verification',
      'pr.verify.b': 'Every figure here reproduces. The fixpoint with <code>tools/fixpoint.sh</code>, the browser page with <code>tools/build-sassembly-web.sh</code>, the guards with <code>cargo test</code>. What has not been measured is not printed here.',
      'pr.contact.h': 'Contact',
      'pr.contact.b': 'Questions, images, interviews — ask in the <a href="https://discord.gg/XvYvXR8HAh" rel="noopener">study group</a>, or open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/paramtatv/sassembly/issues" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>. A question about a specific line works better here than a general one.',
      'pr.foot': 'Every release is published with its measurements.',
      'foot.discord': 'Discord',
      'comm.h': 'Read the compiler together',
      'comm.b': 'A study group for Sassembly developers on Discord — reading the compiler, asking questions, dividing the work. Everyone is welcome.',
      'comm.cta': 'Join the study group',
      'comm.note': 'a compiler meant to be read is a compiler meant to be read together',
